
This directory is the default location for static OpenIFS data files.

The data files can be downloaded from here:
https://openifs.ecmwf.int/data/ifsdata/48r1/

Please download the following tarballs into this directory:

 ifsdata/ifsdata.tar.gz
 rtables/rtables.tar.gz
 climate.v020/48r1_climate.v020_${RES}.tar.gz
   where ${RES} represents the horizontal grid resolutions you intend to use

Following this extract the data packages into their respective subdirectories:

 tar -xzf ifsdata.tar.gz -C ./ifsdata
 tar -xzf rtables.tar.gz -C ./rtables
 tar -xzf 48r1_climate.v020_${RES}.tar.gz -C ./climate.v020

Note: Depending on the number of extracted model grids, the data volume of
the downloaded packages can be large. By default you will be adding this data
in the $OIFS_HOME/openifs-data location. Please ensure that you have sufficient
disk space available. Otherwise you can replace this directory with a symbolic
link to a different location on your file system.

